== Diagnoses ==

1+2. DOOR DROPS (test-side): apiclient fanOut is fire-and-forget — a handler
   more than handlerQueueDepth=256 (internal/apiclient/client.go) behind
   silently drops. Back-to-back 1000/300-push bursts outrun the feed
   goroutine exactly on slow shared 2-core runners (last=941 / last=256).
   Documented product policy, not ring lossage; the tests asserted ring
   semantics through a lossy door. Fix: door-safe waves (200/wave, absorbed
   between waves via waitLastSeq) — every original assertion kept exact.

3. PRODUCT-SIDE ordering defect (fixed in 4bfc7f4): the merged view sorted
   by receive timestamp, stable — the failure pattern [2,6|4|5|1,3] is four
   per-source blocks in map-iteration order: ALL SIX events shared ONE Ts
   (Windows monotonic clock ~15.6ms tick; the 6-event burst landed inside a
   single tick) and the stable sort kept the map concatenation order.
   ring.go's comment claimed "equal-timestamp events keep arrival order" —
   false across sources. A real Windows daemon misorders events_recent's
   merged view within a clock tick. Fix: per-board arrival counter stamped
   at append (under es.mu, unexported, never crosses JSON); recent() sorts
   by it. Regression tests: ring_test.go (equal-Ts interleave x50 reads,
   limit cut, eviction leg; per-source cap leg).

4. UNSATISFIABLE WAIT (test-side): probeUntilLive returned when ANY session
   notified; a straggler session's registration settled later, missed every
   probe notification, and nothing further was ever pushed — the follow-up
   waitAllRecs(base,1) could never satisfy on a loaded runner. Fix:
   probeUntilAllLive (probes until EVERY session >=1, door-safe 64-probe
   waves with absorb) and no wait between it and the first event.
   HintReArmsAfterDelivery also restructured: delivery-window catch by
   RETRY (gate each A on landing via `appended`, then spin for the
   dequeued-but-flying state; missed windows retry with a fresh event) —
   the first local loaded-race reproduction showed the naive spin burning
   200 retries in 1.7s reading the PRE-ARM settled state.
   Deadlines: 5s -> evWaitDeadline() = 30s (60s under -race) — the
   deadline fails hung tests, not slow runners (convention 438dc83).

